            "num": 3,
            "title": "List of materials and photo reference",
            "demo": true,
            "materials": [],
            "html_body": "<div class=\"materials-sheet\">\r\n<p class=\"materials-intro\">Materials Angus McEwan uses for the door painting in this course. Lesson 2 shows his working setup in the studio.</p>\r\n<ol class=\"materials-items\">\r\n<li><strong>Paper.</strong> Watercolor paper taped to a board. Angus works on a vertical surface so washes can run; keep paper towels along the bottom edge of the board.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Paints.</strong> Angus typically paints with Daniel Smith watercolors. His core palette:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Van Dyke Brown</li>\r\n<li>Burnt Umber</li>\r\n<li>Prussian Blue</li>\r\n<li>Cobalt Blue</li>\r\n<li>Manganese Blue Hue</li>\r\n<li>Lavender</li>\r\n<li>Cobalt Teal Blue</li>\r\n<li>Indian Yellow</li>\r\n<li>Organic Vermillion</li>\r\n<li>Quinacridone Burnt Orange</li>\r\n<li>Chinese White</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><strong>Gold acrylic</strong> for the bolts.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Watercolor crayons</strong> (Caran d’Ache Neocolor II or similar) for texture and light.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Brushes.</strong> A range of rounds, including a small pointed brush for the final details.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Sponge</strong> to build surface texture.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Cardboard / card</strong> to print shapes (the numbers on the door).</li>\r\n<li><strong>Pencil</strong> for the preparatory drawing and to restore lines after washes.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Spray bottle with water</strong> to smooth and move the texture layers.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Paper tape, paper towels,</strong> and a water can.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div class=\"reference-panel\">\r\n<h3>Photo reference</h3>\r\n<p>The door Angus paints in this lesson — rusted bolts, flaking blue paint, and the number 06.</p>\r\n<div class=\"reference-media\"><img src=\"/assets/courses/angus/door-reference.jpg\" alt=\"Reference: blue door with rusted bolts\"></div>\r\n<a class=\"reference-download\" href=\"/assets/courses/angus/door-reference.jpg\" download=\"angus-mcewan_door.jpg\">Download reference image</a>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>"
        },
